  "title": "Images keep their edges",
  "summary": "June made image and text requests more useful while giving the growing community project directory a clearer shape.\n\nGPT Image gained transparent PNG output through `transparent=true`, including for edits. Repeated in-flight requests can share a generation, and a semantic cache can reuse results for similar prompts.\n\nThe catalog added O3 with image input and search options, updated DeepSeek reasoning and the `llama` alias, and put GPT-4.1 Nano in the anonymous tier. Requests without an explicit model now use that faster `openai-fast` option.\n\nThe directory was reorganized into seven categories as community additions continued across creative tools, bots, games, and app-building. CraftUI became the first Vibe Coding entry.\n\nText ads began respecting account preferences and conversation history without replacing answers. Queue rules gained clearer tier distinctions, token validation was shortened, and content-free performance tracking was added for text generation.",
